* Generic (non-PDK) NMOS + PMOS corner models standing in for sky130's own
* tt/ss/ff process split -- same "runs anywhere ngspice runs" precedent as
* examples/kb/rc-relaxation-oscillator/corners.lib. VTO/KP/LAMBDA move
* together the way a real sky130 corner split would move a device's drive
* strength and output resistance. The NMOS cards are identical to the
* easy-tier tasks' own models.lib; the PMOS cards are this (medium) tier's
* addition -- a complementary cascode load cannot be built without one.
* Replace with a real sky130 model library (models.pdk / models.lib
* pointing at $PDK_ROOT) once this task is re-run against real devices --
* see README.md "Known limitation" note.
.model bench_nmos NMOS(LEVEL=1 VTO=0.55 KP=100u LAMBDA=0.04)
.model bench_pmos PMOS(LEVEL=1 VTO=-0.60 KP=40u LAMBDA=0.05)

.lib tt
.model bench_nmos NMOS(LEVEL=1 VTO=0.50 KP=120u LAMBDA=0.05)
.model bench_pmos PMOS(LEVEL=1 VTO=-0.55 KP=45u LAMBDA=0.06)
.endl tt

.lib ss
.model bench_nmos NMOS(LEVEL=1 VTO=0.60 KP=95u LAMBDA=0.04)
.model bench_pmos PMOS(LEVEL=1 VTO=-0.65 KP=36u LAMBDA=0.05)
.endl ss

.lib ff
.model bench_nmos NMOS(LEVEL=1 VTO=0.40 KP=145u LAMBDA=0.06)
.model bench_pmos PMOS(LEVEL=1 VTO=-0.45 KP=55u LAMBDA=0.07)
.endl ff
